# Sensor noise for batch fault runs, loaded by ga_faults.run after batch.parm
# (skip with --no-noise). What this SITL build can actually do, from its sources:
#   SIM_GYRn_RND   deg/s, uniform, scaled by throttle (~0.4 at hover). Mostly
#                  removed by ArduPilot's 20 Hz gyro filter, so the effect is small.
#   SIM_BARO_RND   m, random height noise - clearly visible in the log
#   SIM_GPS1_VERR  m/s, uniform random GPS velocity error per axis
#   SIM_GPS1_NOISE m, slow sine on GPS altitude
# Not used:
#   SIM_ACCn_RND   only scales the vibration models (SIM_VIB_FREQ / SIM_VIB_MOT_MAX),
#                  it adds no random accel noise on its own
#   horizontal GPS position noise - this SITL GPS model has none
# SITL never seeds its random generator, so every run gets the same noise
# sequence; the runner varies the fault time to get run-to-run spread.

SIM_GYR1_RND    1.5
SIM_GYR2_RND    1.5
SIM_BARO_RND    0.2
SIM_BAR2_RND    0.2
SIM_GPS1_VERR_X 0.1
SIM_GPS1_VERR_Y 0.1
SIM_GPS1_VERR_Z 0.1
SIM_GPS1_NOISE  0.3
